# Module complete = one commit (code + dashboard + bugs)

After a module is **genuinely complete**, update these three in the **same commit** as the test code — never as a later follow-up:

1. Test code (page objects, tests, suite XML)
2. GitHub Pages dashboard (`docs/coverage.json`, `docs/index.html`, and any related `docs/` pages)
3. `BUGS_FOUND.docx` — only if new bugs were found on that module (append; do not mark bugs Fixed unless the user verified)

## Gate (all required)

A module is complete only when:

- Tests are written
- Tests have been run on the real device/emulator
- The user has **confirmed the results**

Do not update the dashboard or bug doc from projected/assumed results. Do not ship dashboard/bug-doc updates before user confirmation.

## Do not leave them out of sync

Never commit test code for a finished module while leaving the dashboard or bug doc stale. Never update the dashboard/bug doc in a separate later step after the test commit.

If the user has not confirmed yet, stop after the evidence report and wait.

## BUGS_FOUND numbering — one row per page finding

Do **not** merge bugs across screens even when the pattern is the same (offline UX, a11y checkbox, rapid-tap, etc.). Each page that shows the defect gets its **own sequential number**.

- Sign up offline Get OTP = one row; OTP offline Submit = next row; OTP offline Resend = next row.
- Never fold a later page into an earlier row ("same family as #8").
- Number strictly 1, 2, 3… in the order found. Do not reuse or collapse numbers.
